From: AMI Meta Layer <meta-ami>
Subject: [PATCH] Combined patches for phosphor-software-manager

This patch combines all AMI-specific modifications to phosphor-software-manager
including support for firmware update features, security enhancements, and Intel
platform-specific functionality.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AMI-specific customizations]

Changes included:

1. Patch 0001: Add Purpose for other components and image-mtd support
   - Add VersionPurpose::Other for non-BMC/BIOS components
   - Support for image-mtd firmware images

2. Patch 0003: Non-PFR dual image inventory population support
   - Dual image inventory management for non-PFR platforms

3. Patch 0004: Add write public key in image support
   - Extract and store public keys from flash images
   - Support public key verification workflow

4. Patch 0005: Add support to ApplyTime property
   - Implement maintenance window scheduling for firmware updates
   - Add Task D-Bus interface with ApplyTime support
   - Support Immediate and AtMaintenanceWindowStart apply times
   - Create task.hpp and task.cpp for timer-based update scheduling

5. Patch 0005-nonpfr: Remove image when verification fails
   - Clean up uploaded images on verification failure
   - Increment activeUpdatesCount and call onFlashWriteFailure

6. Patch 0006: Delete Update image dbus path on success or failure
   - Add activeUpdatesCount tracking and performReboot flag
   - Implement onFlashWriteFailure method
   - Split onFlashWriteSuccess into FWUPD_SCRIPT and non-FWUPD_SCRIPT sections
   - Create activationBlocksTransition D-Bus object

7. Patch 0007: Fixed core dump issue while verifying unsigned images
   - Comment out HOST_BIOS_UPGRADE section to prevent core dumps
   - Handle unsigned image verification gracefully

8. Patch 0008: Clear tmp and firmware inventory while cancel task
   - Add isTaskCancelled flag to Task class
   - Clean up resources when update task is cancelled
   - Call onFlashWriteFailure on task cancellation

9. Patch 0009: Fixed Firmware update security issue - Unsafe Unpacking
   - Add firmware file validation after untar operation
   - Check for path traversal attacks (relative paths with "..")
   - Verify no execute permissions on extracted files
   - Validate all files against allowed firmware file list
   - Mount /tmp/images with tmpfs using nosuid,noexec options

10. Patch 0010-nonpfr: Add condition to skip removal of BMC obj path
    - Preserve bmc_active and bmc_bkup default BMC versions
    - Skip removal of default BMC inventory objects

11. Patch 0011: Add HttpPushUriTarget and busy property
    - Add FirmwareUpdateTarget D-Bus interface
    - Support HttpPushUriTarget and busy properties

Files Modified (12 files):
  - bmc/task.cpp: NEW - Task timer implementation for scheduled updates
  - bmc/task.hpp: NEW - Task class with ApplyTime support
  - bmc/activation.cpp: ApplyTime, task management, failure handling
  - bmc/activation.hpp: Public interface changes, onFlashWriteFailure
  - bmc/image_manager.cpp: Firmware security validation
  - bmc/image_verify.cpp: Public key extraction from flash
  - bmc/images.hpp: Firmware file validation list
  - bmc/item_updater.cpp: Default BMC version preservation
  - bmc/item_updater.hpp: FirmwareUpdateTarget interface, activeUpdatesCount
  - bmc/meson.build: Build and updater source configuration
     - bmc/static/flash.cpp: FWUPD_SCRIPT flow handling in unit state changes
  - bmc/xyz.openbmc_project.Software.Version.service.in: tmpfs security mount

Signed-off-by: AMI <meta-ami>
---
